    "chunk_size_bytes": 1871,
    "chunk_text": "(ii)produce any foreign fishing boats seized or detained as the case may beunder this Act with the crew where such boat is not abandoned, beforethe Magistrate instead of High-Court in order to overcome practicaldifficulties; and\n\n(2)to transfer the authority of the Director or the Government agent to the DirectorGeneral.\n\nClause 6 : This clause amends section 15 of the principal enactment and the legal effectof the section as amended is to impose enhanced fines based on the length of the fishingboat for the offences committed contravening section 4 and section 5 of the Act in theterritorial waters and the Exclusive Economic Zone of Sri Lanka.\n\nClause 7 : This clause amends section 16 of the principal enactment and the legal effectof the section as amended is to enable the Magistrates to exercise power in respect ofoffences committed under this Act, and to enhance the fine in respect of violation ofconditions of a permit by a foreign fishing boat.\n\nClause 8 : This clause amends section 17 of the principal enactment and the legal effectof the section as amended is to enable Magistrates to exercise power in respect of enhancedfines for the offence of obstructing authorized officers, taking into consideration thelength of the fishing boat.\n\nClause 9 : This clause inserts new section 17A to the principal enactment and the legaleffect of the section as amended is to make all offences committed under this Act cognizableand non-bailable.\n\nClause 10 : This clause amends section 18 of the principal enactment and is consequentialto the amendment made by clause 8.\n\nClause 11 : This clause amends section 19 of the principal enactment and the legaleffect of the section as amended is to enable High Court to hear the original appeals givingan opportunity to be heard again by Court of Appeal and to change the designation ofDirector as the Director General."
