    "chunk_text": "Clause 11 : This clause amends section 19 of the principal enactment and the legaleffect of the section as amended is to enable High Court to hear the original appeals givingan opportunity to be heard again by Court of Appeal and to change the designation ofDirector as the Director General.\n\nClause 13 : This clause amends section 20 of the principal enactment and the legaleffect of the section as amended is to provide for the imposition of a penalty by theDirector General for offences committed for the first time in the Exclusive EconomicZone together with procedure to be adhered to.\n\nClause 14 : This clause amends section 20 of the principal enactment by the insertionof new section 20A to the principal enactment and the legal effect of the section asamended is to provide for the appointment of a panel of experts.\n\nClause 15 : This clause amends section 21 of the principal enactment and the legaleffect of the section as amended is to provide for the release of any boat on the provisionof a satisfactory bond or security until the conclusion of any prosecution and to enable theMagistrate to exercise powers in respect of offences committed under this Act.\n\nClause 16 : This clause amends section 23 of the principal enactment and the legaleffect of the section as amended is to make provision for the presumption, on violation ofthe provisions of the Act where a foreign fishing boat is found in Sri Lanka Waters.\n\nClause 17 : This clause amends section 24 of the principal enactment and the legaleffect of the section as amended is to enable the Magistrate to exercise powers in respect ofoffences committed under this Act.\n\nClause 18 : This clause amends section 26 of the principal enactment and the legaleffect of the section as amended is to widen the regulation making power for theimplementation of standards stipulated in International conventions and agreements."
