    "chunk_text": "13.Section 20 of the principal enactment is herebyrepealed and the following section substituted therefor:-\n\n20. (1) Where the Director-General hassufficient evidence to believe that any personhas acted in contravention of the provisions ofthis Act, he may\u2013\n\n(b)having regard to the circumstances inwhich such contravention has takenplace,\n\nif it is appropriate to impose a penalty, cause anotice to be served in the prescribed form onsuch person, requiring him to appear withinone month from the date of receipt of suchnotice and show cause why a penalty shouldnot be imposed on him.\n\nReplacementof section 20of theprincipalenactment.\u201cCompoundingof offences.\n\nWhen toconsider anabandonedforeignfishing boatas a foreignfishing boat.\n\n10Fisheries (Regulation of Foreign Fishing Boats)(Amendment)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n(2) Where the person on whom the notice isserved appears within one month from the dateof receipt of such notice and admits that heacted in contravention of the provisions of thisAct, the Director-General shall impose on thatperson a penalty not exceeding one third of themaximum penalty that could be imposed underthis Act to which such person could be liable topay.\n\n(3) Where a person on whom notice is servedwithin one month from the date of receipt ofsuch notice states that he has a cause to showagainst the imposition of the penalty, theDirector General may preceed forthwith to hearand decide the matter in the manner prescribed.\n\n(4) Where the Director- General is notsatisfied with reasons given he may afterassigning his own reasons therefore, impose thepenalty specified in subsection (2) of thissection.\n\n(5) Where the Director-General imposes apenalty on any person under this section heshall cause a notice in the prescribed form to beserved on such person indicating particulars ofsuch penalty."
