    "chunk_text": "(6) (a) Nothing in this section shall be construed toprevent the Commission from entering into an agreementwith any person on the basis of an admission of liability topay an amount not exceeding three times the gross amountof the pecuniary gain made or loss avoided calculated foreach offence on the basis provided for under this section fora contravention of any provision of this Part; and\n\n(7) Subsections (2) and (3) shall mutatis mutandis applyin relation to sums of money recovered by the Commissionunder subsections (4), (5) and (6) of this section.\n\n(8) Any right of action that is conferred under this sectionshall not affect the right of action that is conferred on aperson who has suffered loss or damage referred to in anyother section of this Act or under any other law.\n\nPART VI\n\nFINANCE\n\n150.The object and purpose of this Part shall be \u2013\n\n(a) to establish various funds for the properfunctioning of the Commission; and\n\n(b) to establish a fund to provide limitedcompensation to investors who have no otherremedy.\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\nObject andpurpose ofthis Part.\n\nSecurities Exchange129\n\nCHAPTER 1\n\nFunds of the Commission\n\n151.(1) There shall be charged, levied and paid a cessat such rates as may be prescribed by the Minister by way ofregulations published in the Gazette on every purchase andsale of securities recorded in an exchange or notified to itunder its rules by both the purchaser and the seller. Differentrates may be prescribed in respect of different classes ofsecurities.\n\n(2) The cess imposed under this section shall be inaddition to any other tax or cess levied under any other law.\n\n152.(1) There shall be established a fund called theCess Fund to which shall be credited the proceeds of thecess imposed under section 151.\n\n(2) There shall be paid out of the Cess Fund such sums asmay be authorized by the Commission for the purpose of \u2013\n\n(a)developing the securities market;"
