    "chunk_text": "PARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\nCOMMERCIAL MEDIATION CENTRE OFSRI LANKA (AMENDMENT)\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nPresented by the Minister of Foreign Employment and Minister of Justiceon 21st of November, 2017\n\n(Published in the Gazette on November 06, 2017)\n\nOrdered by Parliament to be printed\n\nto amend the Commercial Mediation Centre of Sri LankaAct, No. 44 of 2000\n\n2\u2014PL 010477\u2014510 (11/2017)\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n[Bill No. 216]\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nPrice : Rs. 12.00Postage : Rs. 10.00\n\nThis Bill can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\nSTATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT\n\nClause 2 : This clause amends section 5 of the Commercial Mediation Centre ofSri Lanka Act, No. 44 of 2000 (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d), and thelegal effect of the section as amended is to increase the number of members of the Board ofManagement of the Commercial Mediation Centre with a view to ensuring better co-ordinationamong the line agencies.\n\nClause 3 : This clause amends section 6 of the principal enactment and the legal effect ofthe section as amended is to enable the Minister to appoint the Chairman of the Board ofManagement and to specify the manner by which the Chairman can be removed from office.\n\n1Commercial Mediation Centre of Sri Lanka(Amendment)\n\nShort title.\n\nL.D.\u2014O. 29/2017\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE COMMERCIAL MEDIATION CENTRE OFSRI LANKA ACT, NO. 44 OF 2000\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2013\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Commercial MediationCentre of Sri Lanka (Amendment) Act, No. of 2017.\n\n2.Section 5 of the Commercial Mediation Centre ofSri Lanka Act, No. 44 of 2000 (hereinafter referred to as the\u201cprincipal enactment\u201d) is hereby amended as follows:\u2013\n\n(1)in subsection (1) thereof,\u2013"
